module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, NamedField, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the seed Rust emitter decides that a two-argument type lowers to the host keyed container (HashMap) from the authored LEAF SPELLING at the position (`v1.compiler.types` `node_is_keyed_collection`: the declared alias roster, plus `node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling`, which reads the algebra row for the spelling), not from the declaration the position resolves to. Any other declaration whose leaf is FinitelySupportedFunction, or an alias spelling shadowed by a user type, lowers to HashMap. gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate: type compatibility keys on the exact declaration a position resolves to, never its leaf name.",

    "HARM AND SPECIMEN: operator Map ruling of 2026-10-21 (its gunbc.design_ruling row lands with #14876, the atomic cutover this PR is the prerequisite of; it is not in this tree, so it is not a DeclarationRef here). Retyping std.algebra to spell FinitelySupportedFunction directly rendered the algebra struct beside HashMap callers (32 E0308 in the regenerated std_algebra.rs and std_source_annotation.rs), because the spelling is deliberately not an alias row (canonical_spelling_sorts_ahead_of_alias_reason). The admitted repair reads the spelling from the declared algebra rows and admits only the keyed algebra; it stays at spelling grain because the emitter reaches only the authored name at that site. Same class as host_seam_realization_is_keyed_by_primitive_spelling (sunny-bee-153, lands with #14751); a receipt for this site belongs on that row once it lands.",

    "LATENT DIVERGENCE ON MAIN FOUND BY THIS REPAIR, WITH BEFORE/AFTER MIRROR LINES (heal commit fb91c4b3976): the declared alias `type Map<Key, Value> = FinitelySupportedFunction<Key, Value>` in std.types emitted `pub type Map<Key, Value> = Rc<crate::std_algebra::FinitelySupportedFunction<Key, Value>>;` (the algebra PROFILE STRUCT), while every kernel Map position lowered to `Rc<HashMap<K, V>>`; the same split sat in the profile struct's own fields (`pub empty: Rc<FinitelySupportedFunction<K, V>>`, `insert`, `merge` in std_algebra.rs). After: std_types.rs `pub type Map<Key, Value> = Rc<HashMap<Key, Value>>;` and std_algebra.rs `pub empty: Rc<HashMap<K, V>>` with insert and merge to match. No value crossed the two representations at runtime because no stage0 consumer built the struct form (a value of it could not flow into a HashMap parameter, which is why the retyped std.algebra failed rustc with 32 E0308 until the rule landed), and the three mirrors (std_algebra.rs, std_types.rs, v1_compiler_infer_types.rs) are regenerated together in one bot commit. The class: one concept, two emitted representations, keyed by which spelling the declaration was authored with.",

    "SECOND CONSUMER OF THE SAME CLASSIFIER: `v1.compiler.resolve` `is_user_generic_use_site` also reads `node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling`, so the resolver decides keyed-container-ness from the authored leaf spelling too (a user type spelled FinitelySupportedFunction takes the keyed path; the witness fixture's stand-in declaration exercises exactly this because a fixture manifest has no corpus roots to import std.algebra from). Fork census: two sites, the emitter and the resolver, both reading the one predicate, so the rule is not duplicated, only its spelling key is shared. The fixture asserts the dispatch route, not that a foreign declaration should be admitted; it is deleted-or-rekeyed with the trigger.",

    "THIRD CONSUMER, FOUND BY THE #14876 HEAL ROUND (E0609 no field `map_keys` on Rc<im::HashMap<K, V>> at the generated map_support_keys): `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `rust_receiver_has_callable_method_field` asked whether the receiver's record declares an arrow field of the method name. std.algebra declares FinitelySupportedFunction as the profile struct with a `map_keys: fn() -> FreeMonoid<K>` member, so a receiver spelled FinitelySupportedFunction (lowered to HashMap) answered yes and `m |> map_keys` emitted the field call `(m.map_keys)()`. It now answers no for a receiver node_is_keyed_collection lowers to the host container, reading the same predicate as the other two sites. The pre-existing comment on that function records the same defect for the Map spelling, widened through the container template algebra.",

    "CENSUS AND A FALSE POSITIVE (gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization root generalization, PR #14951). KEYED IS NOT LOWERED: node_is_keyed_collection classifies the SPELLING (a container alias row plus arity 2), and `PartialFunction<K, V>` passes it while having no Rust host inhabitant, so it renders as its record. Exempting the callable-field tier on node_is_keyed_collection alone sent `tree.facts |> lookup(node)` in v2.compiler.eval inferred_facts_witness_for_eval to the HashMap lookup (E0308 at the emitted v2_compiler_eval.rs, #14951 v2-bootstrap at 9fd0ffb). The tier now also asks `v1.compiler.emit` `keyed_container_has_target_inhabitant`, the coerce_container_template fact emit_keyed_container_type branches on, so the exemption and the type renderer read one fact; a PartialFunction record control holds it. Sites that ask about representation must ask that target fact, not keyed-ness. Two sites still compare the bare leaf `Map` and are left as CANDIDATES, not changed, because widening them to node_is_keyed_collection would carry the same PartialFunction false positive: `v1.compiler.infer_lookup` `map_lookup_result_type` and `v1.compiler.infer` `expected_collection_surface`. They are retired by the same next-rung trigger below. Every other record-versus-keyed branch in resolve / infer / lookup / emit / emit_rust already routes through node_is_keyed_collection.",

    "SECOND INSTANCE, THE TYPE POSITION RATHER THAN THE CONTAINER LITERAL (bold-stag-227, 2026-11-09, found while cutting the positional DESIGN citations over; the verbs that drove it are PR #16134). STATEMENT: `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `rust_render_type_leaf_name` (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag:3309) renders a type-position leaf as `()` when `is_value_variant_type_arg` (src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag:1483) finds that leaf in `emit_info.variant_to_enum`, and the map is folded over the WHOLE TRANSITIVE closure by `derive_variant_to_enum` (src/v1/04_emit_info.dag:863), keyed by the variant's leaf spelling — its own comment reads variant leaf to the key of the enum that declares it, or the empty string when two enums declare that variant. A record declared in one module and a unit arm declared in another therefore answer as a variant at every position of the emission, so the same declaration renders differently depending on what else the closure happens to reach.",

    "SPECIMEN, AND THE ASYMMETRY THAT PROVES THE KEY IS PRESENCE AND NOT IDENTITY: `Edge` is declared as a record exactly once, `type Edge { label: EdgeLabel; target: Node; declaration: EdgeDeclaration }` at src/v2/std/node.dag:348, and occurs once more anywhere in the tree, as the unit arm `Edge` of `type HoldGraspKind` at dag/extdeps/climbing_holds/types.dag:209. With the arm's module OUT of the emitted closure (the 233-module v2 CLI closure on main) the emitted crate carries `pub struct Edge` at v2_std_node.rs:428 and `pub fn core_edge(...) -> Rc<Edge>`, and it compiles. With the arm's module IN, the SAME file emits `pub struct Edge` unchanged and `-> Rc<()>` at the use sites — v2_std_node.rs:339, and `Rc<Vec<Rc<()>>>` at :458 and :476, 77 sites in that file — while the expression position keeps writing `Edge`, which is why only the type position is wrong and the declaration looks healthy. The surviving counts are 59 E0308, 38 E0609 and 17 E0631 in the emitted crate. Because exactly one coproduct claims the name, the fold records it unambiguously instead of writing the empty string it reserves for a name two enums claim: a SECOND claimant would have saved the build. Presence of a spelling decides, never which declaration it denotes — the same defect as `host_seam_realization_is_keyed_by_primitive_spelling`, one rung further in.",

    "THE PER-FILE ANSWER ALREADY EXISTS IN THE SAME FILE: the emitter's own comment at src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag:1471-1482 records that ownership of a constructor name is a per-file fact — `v1.compiler.infer` `constructor_binding_authority` answers from the file's own declarations plus its direct imports, and a name owned twice in one file is refused as VariantCollision — while the map this path consults flattens that per-file fact across the closure. The coproduct-declaration position at src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag:2749 already carries the guard; the type position does not. RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder for the type position, because nothing between the emitter and the host toolchain refuses — the emitted crate simply does not compile, and the lane reports it as EmittedCompilerBuildFailed rather than as a refusal with a cause. CEILING: structurally guaranteed once the type-position lookup asks the same per-file constructor question. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: that lookup reads the resolved declaration, with a witness claim pinning both directions — a leaf that is a record of this file renders its name even when a coproduct elsewhere in the closure has an arm of that spelling, and a genuine unit arm still renders `()`. warm-bear-654 dispatched the emitter repair as its own work item on 2026-11-09; it is not repaired here, and this row does not claim it is.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (spelling-keyed, no collision refusal). CEILING: structurally guaranteed once the emitter reads the resolved declaration identity at the position. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the emitter at node_is_keyed_collection AND the resolver at is_user_generic_use_site carry the resolved declaration (the one representation classifier of the Map crossing, PR 2 of the Map ruling), so the alias roster and the algebra spelling collapse to one row read keyed on std.algebra.FinitelySupportedFunction.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.design_ruling", decl_name: "text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "FinitelySupportedFunction", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "Edge", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.climbing_holds.types", decl_name: "HoldGraspKind", field: NamedField { field_name: "Edge" } },
  ],
}
